    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "engine.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add is_int_digit. The body is one expression: ch.is_ascii_digit() || ('\\u{FF10}'..='\\u{FF19}').contains(&ch). match_int uses that helper in its while loop. Do not change match_hex or match_float. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch highlight_line. The existing test highlight_is_deterministic_and_state_converges stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_fullwidth_digit_is_an_integer builds Prepared from the text U+FF12 and Delimiters::from_chars of an empty slice. match_int at offset 0 has end 1. The text 12 has end 2. The text a is None. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
